description:
pkix-path/src/lib.rs:2314–2334

The code checks nc_constrained_types.contains(NC_TYPE_RFC822) twice:

1. To compute permitted_rfc822_vec (else branch produces GeneralSubtrees::default())
2. To compute permitted_rfc822: Option<&[...]> (else branch produces None)

The else branch in step 1 allocates an empty GeneralSubtrees only to be wrapped in None in step 2. The two bindings can be collapsed: when NC_TYPE_RFC822 is not set, neither the Vec nor the Option is needed. The idiomatic form is one binding that directly produces Option<GeneralSubtrees>, testing the condition once:

    let permitted_rfc822_vec: Option<GeneralSubtrees> =
        nc_constrained_types.contains(NC_TYPE_RFC822).then(|| {
            nc_permitted
                .map(|p| p.iter().filter(|st| matches!(st.base, GeneralName::Rfc822Name(_))).cloned().collect())
                .unwrap_or_default()
        });
    let permitted_rfc822 = permitted_rfc822_vec.as_deref();

This removes the duplicate condition check and the dead default() allocation.
